# Semgrep ignore for BersonCareBot (SEC-01 / task #881, part of security.yml `semgrep` job).
#
# Purpose: keep Semgrep's SAST scan focused on hand-written source. Everything here is either
# vendored/installed, machine-generated, a build artifact, or a data/fixture blob — scanning it
# wastes CI time and produces noise, not real findings. Mirrors `.gitignore` plus a few
# Semgrep-specific carve-outs (generated DB migration snapshots, test fixtures).
#
# Semgrep also respects .gitignore automatically, but we keep this file explicit and
# self-contained so the exclusion list is auditable in one place without cross-referencing.

# --- Dependencies / vendored -----------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# --- Build outputs -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
**/dist/
**/build/
.next/
**/.next/
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
apps/webapp/out/

# --- Test coverage ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
**/coverage/

# --- Minified / bundled JS ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.min.js
**/*.min.js

# --- Lockfiles (not source, huge, no actionable SAST signal) --------------------------------
pnpm-lock.yaml
**/pnpm-lock.yaml

# --- Generated DB migration snapshots (drizzle-kit metadata, not hand-written code) ----------
apps/webapp/db/drizzle-migrations/meta/
**/drizzle-migrations/meta/

# --- Test fixtures (demo/synthetic data, not app logic — memory: demo-test-fixtures-on-test-db)
apps/integrator/e2e/fixtures/
apps/webapp/public/test-fixtures/
apps/webapp/src/modules/saas-test-fixture/
**/fixtures/
**/test-fixtures/

# --- Local agent tooling / transient working files (never committed, but excluded defensively)
.claude/
.tmp/
